<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 21.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 21.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended June 21</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     360	   0.22     395300  142.31    3.19</p>
<p>Telco		  450	   1.86     217100   97.70   21.55</p>
<p>TISCO		  193	   0.67     445900   86.06   18.10</p>
<p>ITC		    505	   1.96     135200   68.28   20.24</p>
<p>HDFC		  3460	  14.90	17980   62.21   22.45</p>
<p>ACC		   1210	   5.10	41970   50.78   21.98</p>
<p>BHEL		   390	   1.65	90100   35.14   22.06</p>
<p>STERLITE	     270	   1.14     128000   34.56   22.02</p>
<p>MTNL		   300	   1.28     111700   33.51   22.25</p>
<p>HLL		   1320	   5.02	23400   30.89   19.83</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 21.42 percent on an annualised basis against 27.67 percent in the previous carry forward account ended June 14.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
